message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Shift Intent Left: Intent Contracts, Agency Budgets, and Drift Verification for Securing the Agentic Software Development Lifecycle"
abstract: >-
  Shift left moved security activities toward the earliest artifact of the
  software development lifecycle: source code. Autonomous coding agents
  invalidate the premise that code is that earliest artifact, because an agent
  takes security-relevant actions before any diff exists. This work argues that
  the earliest securable artifact in an agentic SDLC is intent, and introduces
  Shift Intent Left (SIL): a lifecycle discipline that makes intent explicit,
  bounded and verifiable before execution, and checks execution against it
  afterwards.
